  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROTECTING AND MONITORING THE SUMATRAN TIGER POPULATION OF THE BUKIT TIGA PULUH NATIONAL PARK IN SUMATRA, INDONESIA.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO (1) CONDUCT JOINT PATROLS BETWEEN PARK RANGERS AND COMMUNITY-BASED SCOUTS (2) IMPLEMENT SMART (SPATIAL MONITORING AND REPORTING TOOL) PATROLS AND PROVIDE LAW ENFORCEMENT TRAINING TO SIGNIFICANTLY REDUCE TIGER POACHING, ILLEGAL LOGGING, AND FOREST ENCROACHMENT (3) MONITOR TIGERS AND THEIR HABITAT TO ASSESS THE HEALTH OF THE ECOSYSTEM AND CONSERVATION STATUS THROUGHOUT THE PROJECT LIFESPAN (4) SECURE THE LIVELIHOOD OF TRADITIONAL AND INDIGENOUS COMMUNITIES IN A SPECIFIC AREA INSIDE THE NATIONAL PARK AS A SAFEGUARD AGAINST CONTINUOUS FOREST ENCROACHMENT IN FAVOR OF FARM LAND (5) BUILD CAPACITY OF TRADITIONAL COMMUNITIES TO SUSTAINABLY IMPLEMENT ENVIRONMENTALLY-FRIENDLY AGROFORESTRY INSIDE THE BUKIT TIGA PULUH NATIONAL PARK AND (6) SUPPORT TRADITIONAL COMMUNITIES INSIDE THE BUKIT TIGA PULUH NATIONAL PARK WITH MARKET ACCESS FOR NON-TIMBER FOREST PRODUCTS.</narrative>
  </description>
